From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IamMaxim <g.maxim.stepanoff@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 9 Jun 2026 22:21:25 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] chore: reconcile Cargo.lock with the stripped crate graph

The strip patches each carry a Cargo.lock hunk, but replaying them across the
v1.4.2 -> v1.5.4 gap via git am -3 left the lockfile partially merged (still
listing removed crates: auto_update, ai_onboarding, ahash 0.7, ...). cargo
regenerated the correct stripped graph at build time; this commits that result
so a clean 'just apply' yields a non-dirty, buildable tree.
---
 Cargo.lock | 2722 ++--------------------------------------------------
 1 file changed, 106 insertions(+), 2616 deletions(-)

